.TH TTYPROBE 1
.SH NAME
ttyprobe \- exercise terminal attribute and ioctl behavior
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttyprobe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ttyprobe
is a guest regression probe for kernel-backed terminal state. It opens a
pseudo-terminal and checks default termios flags, echo control, raw reads,
Ctrl-C data delivery when ISIG is disabled, Ctrl-D EOF handling, window-size
ioctl behavior, foreground process-group ioctls, and ENOTTY failures on
non-terminal descriptors.
